+### Ontology-sensitive review selection (proposed integration)
+
+The [Ontology Reviewer role](../roles/Ontology-Reviewer.md) and [Prompt Skill](../../skills/prompt/SKILL.md) already distinguish the **review domain** (conceptual identities, categories, relationships, ownership, authority and lifecycles) from the **review mode** (exploratory pre-build versus post-build conformance). When a bounded change materially affects those meanings, select an ontology review at the existing appropriate review point rather than introducing an extra lifecycle phase.
+
+For an unsettled conceptual design, an exploratory ontology review may challenge conflated categories, missing distinctions, boundaries or unnecessary abstractions **before** the Implementation Packet freezes them. For a completed artifact claiming adherence to fixed canonical concepts, use an independent, minimal-context ontology conformance review under Step 10. Normal code/behavioral review still checks separate correctness claims; the ontology specialist does not substitute for it or for human approval.
+
+If no significant conceptual claim is at stake, omit specialist review. If the canonical conceptual model is missing or contradictory, record UNRESOLVED and route clarification to its authorized owner instead of silently creating an ontology. The proposed operational selection rules are in docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md. This integration is under review in Draft PR #4; it does not change role authority or make it a deployed agent.
